=head1 DESCRIPTION

The configuration of your app client for refresh token rotation. When
enabled, your app client issues new ID, access, and refresh tokens when
users renew their sessions with refresh tokens. When disabled, token
refresh issues only ID and access tokens.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Feature => Str

The state of refresh token rotation for the current app client.


=head2 RetryGracePeriodSeconds => Int

When you request a token refresh with C<GetTokensFromRefreshToken>, the
original refresh token that you're rotating out can remain valid for a
period of time of up to 60 seconds. This allows for client-side
retries. When C<RetryGracePeriodSeconds> is C<0>, the grace period is
disabled and a successful request immediately invalidates the submitted
refresh token.



